How To make a DOCK distribution for release.

There are four stages each of which is subdivided into steps.

Steps (for everyone) to finalize development:

.  Run all tests including chemgrid, parallel, and pbsa by defining:
   DELPHI_PATH, MPICH_HOME, OE_LICENSE, and ZAP_HOME.
   If tests fail, debug and/or update tests.
   (Recently, we have been punting on pbsa.)

.  Make sure there are tests for each newly added function.

.  Check for memory leaks and bugs:  make valgrinddock checks the plain dock6
   executable and is a good template.

.  Update manual to reflect new functions and parameters and remove deprecated
   functions and parameters.  Remember to include any new images in docs/images/
   folder.

.  Generate release notes for the web site, eg, docs/new_in_6.9.txt.


Steps to get the repository ready:

.  Coordinate a code freeze with all developers:  releases are planned from
   the master branch; developers can continue work in their branches.

.  Update the version and the release date in src/dock/version.h.

.  Download a clean version of the code on the gold standard machine which was
   hamlet, then as of 6.4 was Glenn, then for 6.8 was george, but as of 6.9 is
   Owens: gcc version 4.8.5 20150623 (Red Hat 4.8.5-16) (GCC) RHELS 7.4 (Maipo).
   Compile all executables and run all tests.  If tests fail, debug tests.

.  Update current tutorials to reflect changes in parameter tree and/or
   changes in functionality:  make updatedocktutorials; cd ..; git diff
   amber_scoring_demo and ligand_sampling_demo tutorials mostly live in
   docs/tutorials except for readme's and script_* which live in tutorials.
   solvent_scoring_demo and mpi_demo live in tutorials.
   The above target is suppose to update the dock6 program inputs and outputs
   in one pass (inputs and outputs of other programs need to be manually updated
   if necessary) and invokes target populatedocktutorials to copy files from
   docs/tutorials to tutorials.
   If things don't look correct after making this once then make it again.
   (As of 6.3 the sphere and grid files are from glenn so only the dock ones may
   have to be rerun.  But Scott has not updated these since 6.6 and maybe should
   have since g77 was changed to gfortran.)

.  Download a clean version of the code on Windows, macOS, and Ubuntu OSs.
   Compile all executables, run all tests and tutorials.  If tests fail, debug
   and/or update tests.  Document differences that result from precision issues,
   platform quirks, etc. in install/test/KNOWN_FAILURES.

.  Update docs/tutorials/index.htm and other tutorial web files.

.  Update FAQ current release question to new release.

.  Create new bug fixes file, eg, docs/bugfixes69/6.9_bugfixes.htm
   and update docs/bugfixes.htm

.  Update docs/index.htm

.  Tag repository; plan to use lightweight tags for prereleases, eg;
   git tag dock6-9-beta
   and annotated tags for releases, eg:
   git tag -a dock6-9-release
   For bugfixes plan to use branching.


Steps to make the tarballs from the repository and to post on the server:

.  Update the DISTRIBUTION_TAG in install/Makefile, eg, dock6-9-beta.

.  Generate tarballs for beta testing.  In install/ directory, Makefile target
   archive_export creates tarballs for the distribution and the web site.  Put
   the tarballs on hamlet and request testing on the list dock5@docking.org.
   Incorporate feedback per stages above and then proceed to the next step.

.  Generate tarballs for distribution:  cd install/; make archive_export;

.  Move code tarball from hamlet to dock folder /var/www/html/distributions;
   rename file to dock.6.X_source.tar.gz for consistency with the web site
   script  (NOTE:  I strongly recommend removing the previous version from
   this directory to another location because dock.compbio does not have
   a great deal of hard drive space.) :

   cd /var/www/html/distributions
   df
   tar zcf /tmp/var.www.html.distributions.tgz .
   df
   scptooak /tmp/var.www.html.distributions.tgz
   rm /tmp/var.www.html.distributions.tgz
   sudo mv ~/tmp/dock6.dock6-9-release.tgz .
   sudo chmod 644 dock6.dock6-9-release.tgz
   sudo ln -s dock6.dock6-9-release.tgz dock.6.9_source.tar.gz

.  Enter /var/www/html/distributions on dock.  Update (1 line) version
   number in retrieve_dock_distribution.html :

   sudo vi retrieve_dock_distribution.html

.  Enter /var/www/cgi-bin/distributions on dock.
   Open file retrieve_dock_distribution.py.  Change the following line:

      if dock_version[:6] == 'dock_6':
          dock_version = 'dock6.X'

      where X = newest version

   Open file retrieve_industry_distribution.py.  Change the following line:

      dock6 = ['dock.6.X_source']

      where X = newest version

   Test for academic distribution by applying for fake license and going
   through downloading process.  Test for industry using the password from the
   test industry license "AAAAAAAAA" on the industry license site and then
   download from the web site
   https://dock.compbio.ucsf.edu/retrieve_industry_distribution.html :

   cd /var/www/cgi-bin/distributions
   tar zcf /tmp/var.www.cgi-bin.distributions.tgz .
   scptooak /tmp/var.www.cgi-bin.distributions.tgz
   rm /tmp/var.www.cgi-bin.distributions.tgz
   sudo vi retrieve_dock_distribution.py retrieve_industry_distribution.py

.  Have an independent third party attempt to download code (just in case).

.  Move to /var/www/html/kuntz.  Update (1 line) index.html to current version :

   cd /var/www/html/kuntz
   tar zcf /tmp/var.www.html.kuntz.tgz .
   scptooak /tmp/var.www.html.kuntz.tgz
   sudo vi index.html
   rm /tmp/var.www.html.kuntz.tgz

.  Enter /var/www/html/kuntz/DOCK_6.  This directory tree is doc/ in the
   repository.  Unwrap the web tarball to update the manual, faq, tutorials, ...
   Remember to double check that the updates are now live on the web site :

   cd /var/www/html/kuntz/DOCK_6
   sudo tar zxf ~/tmp/webarchiveexport.dock6-9-release.tgz


Misc. final steps:

.  Send announcements to dock-fans and developers without release notes.
   Templates:
   http://mailman.docking.org/pipermail/dock-fans/2010-May/002357.html
   http://mailman.docking.org/pipermail/dock-fans/2013-January/002739.html
   http://mailman.docking.org/pipermail/dock-fans/2017-April/003321.html

.  Send an ad to the Amber reflector, Chimera-users, and CCL.
   For CCL it is best to have two empty lines at the head of the message.

.  Celebrate!

